TASK 1 – Understand the Problem and Identify the Objects (4 Marks)
1. Problem Analysis
The Campus Smart-Parking System is designed to manage parking spaces in a university. It allows students, staff, and visitors to park their vehicles. The system allocates a suitable parking slot when a vehicle enters and issues a unique parking ticket. When the vehicle leaves, the system releases the slot and calculates the parking fee based on the vehicle type and parking duration.
The system supports two-wheelers, cars, and electric vehicles. Electric vehicles can use special charging slots and pay additional charging fees. Students and staff with valid monthly passes can park for free, while visitors must pay the parking fee.
2. Inputs and Outputs
Inputs:
Vehicle registration number.
Vehicle type.
Floor and slot information.
Vehicle entry and exit times.
Monthly pass details.
Charging units consumed by electric vehicles.
Outputs:
Allocated parking floor and slot.
Unique parking ticket number.
Parking entry and exit details.
Total parking fee.
Slot availability.
Error message when parking is full or the input is invalid.
